00:00:05.643 --> 00:00:07.060
SPEAKER: In this
quickstart, we'll

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.770
install the Google Cloud
SDK, initialize it,

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:12.800
and run core G Cloud commands
from the command line.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.818
Before you begin, make sure you
have a Google Cloud Platform

00:00:15.818 --> 00:00:17.360
project you can use
and that you have

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.470
Python and the Google Cloud
SDK installed on your system.

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:25.250
Begin by using the gcloud init
command to set up the SDK.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.260
This will prompt you to
log in, and after, will

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.120
open a web browser for you
to do so if you choose y.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.650
Log into your
Google user account

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:34.090
by following the
onscreen prompts

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:37.000
to grant permission access
to Google Cloud resources.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.620
Back in the command line,
select a cloud platform project

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:43.340
to use.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:45.590
And if you have the Google
Compute Engine API enabled,

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:48.620
you can choose a default
Compute Engine zone.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.035
After running these
steps, gcloud init

00:00:51.035 --> 00:00:52.910
confirms that you have
successfully completed

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.070
the necessary set of steps.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.260
To view information about
your SDK installation,

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.590
run the following command.

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:02.650
Use gcloud auth list to display
accounts whose credentials

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.080
are stored locally.

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.480
Use gcloud config list
to see the properties

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.980
of your active SDK config.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.330
Use gcloud info to view
a summary of details

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:14.350
about your Cloud
SDK installation,

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:16.800
including installed SDK
components, the active user

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.433
account and more.

00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:21.600
Finally, you can use gcloud
help to view information

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.310
about gcloud commands
and other topics.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:26.660
[MUSIC PLAYING]

